{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/Match","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/MatchesView","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/init(patterns:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/stateCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/containsMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/firstMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/matches(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(at:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(checkedAt:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift#L29"}},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is the trie of the patterns with two more links per state: the failure link, to the state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the longest proper suffix of the state’s prefix that is also a prefix of some pattern, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the output link, to the nearest state along the failure links at which a pattern ends. A scan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the trie while the text matches and the failure links where it stops matching, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads each symbol of the text once and reports all the matches in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a text of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols with "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matches."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","for match in automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\") {","    print(match.patternIndex, match.range)","}","\/\/ 1 1..<4   (\"she\")","\/\/ 0 2..<4   (\"he\")","\/\/ 3 2..<6   (\"hers\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matches come in order of where they end, and of those ending at one place, longest first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ranges count the text’s symbols from 0. The automaton is built once and is immutable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Symbols are mapped to dense indices at construction, through a 256-entry table when they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a dictionary otherwise, so a scan over bytes, such as a string’s "},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", does no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hashing. When the states times the distinct symbols are few enough, every transition is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precomputed into a table, and a scan takes one load per symbol."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/stateCount":{"title":"stateCount","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/stateCount","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kin